TAP Pitch Shifter: declare the Latency port as an output

tap_pitch.ttl declares port 4 "Latency" as an input control port, but
tap_pitch.c writes the plugin's latency to it in run(). Hosts then show it
as a knob (0 to 16027) that the plugin overwrites. Declare it as an output
control port that reports the latency (lv2:designation lv2:latency, and
the older lv2:reportsLatency property).

--- a/pitch/tap_pitch.ttl
+++ b/pitch/tap_pitch.ttl
@@ -77,10 +77,12 @@
     lv2:maximum 20;
 ],
 [
-    a lv2:InputPort, lv2:ControlPort;
+    a lv2:OutputPort, lv2:ControlPort;
     lv2:index 4;
     lv2:symbol "Latency";
     lv2:name "latency";
+    lv2:designation lv2:latency;
+    lv2:portProperty lv2:reportsLatency, lv2:integer;
     lv2:default 0;
     lv2:minimum 0;
     lv2:maximum 16027;
